Provenance and licences of the parts of this project.

----
stereo_warp.py, stereo_warp_onnx.py, ofx/plugin/stereo_pipeline.cpp

Derived from nunif / iw3 by nagadomi, MIT License.
https://github.com/nagadomi/nunif

Specifically from iw3/backward_warp.py, iw3/utils.py, iw3/mapper.py and
iw3/models/row_flow_v2.py. The arithmetic is kept expression-for-expression
identical where the tests require exact agreement.

The depth sizing rule in ofx/plugin/stereo_pipeline.cpp (autoDepthSize) follows
iw3_ext/depth_file.py, itself following depth_anything_model.batch_preprocess().

----
stereo_inpaint.py

Also derived from nunif / iw3 by nagadomi, MIT License, and to the same
standard: expression-for-expression identical where the tests require exact
agreement.

Specifically from iw3/models/monobw.py, iw3/models/light_inpaint_v1.py,
iw3/monobw_inpaint.py, iw3/base_inpaint.py, iw3/dilation.py,
iw3/backward_warp.py, and from nunif/modules/attention.py, norm.py,
gaussian_filter.py, permute.py.

No inpaint weights are shipped here. iw3_light_inpaint_v1_20250919.pth is
downloaded from the nunif GitHub releases at load time, or read from an existing
nunif checkout.

----
models/row_flow_v2.onnx, models/stereo_warp.onnx

Converted from iw3_row_flow_v2_20240130.pth, nagadomi's own weight, published
from the nunif GitHub releases and not listed among nunif's third-party assets.
Redistribution confirmed with the author.

Note that the cc-by-nc-4.0 restrictions described in iw3/README.md attach to
third-party *depth* models (Depth-Anything V2, Video-Depth-Anything and the
metric variants). This project does not use or ship any of them: depth arrives
from outside.

----
ofx/third_party/onnxruntime/*.h

ONNX Runtime C API headers, v1.28.0, Microsoft Corporation, MIT License.
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

Vendored so the build is reproducible. No ONNX Runtime import library is used
and no link-time dependency exists; the runtime is loaded at run time by
absolute path. See ofx/common/ort_runtime.h for why that matters.

----
The OpenFX headers and the OFX C++ Support library are not vendored. They ship
with DaVinci Resolve, under
C:\ProgramData\Blackmagic Design\DaVinci Resolve\Support\Developer\OpenFX,
and are compiled from there. OpenFX is BSD-licensed by
The Open Effects Association Ltd.

----
The Dubois anaglyph coefficients implement the method of Eric Dubois,
"A projection method to generate anaglyph stereo images" (2001).
